{
  // Live animals are goods like any other: the pasture breeds them, and the
  // slaughterhouse turns them into meat and hides. The non-lethal produce
  // (milk, wool, eggs, feathers, honey, wax) skips this step and comes
  // straight from the improvement, see data/resources/animals/animals.json.
  // The raw animal on the hex (data/resources/animals) is the SPAWN, the
  // live_* product here is the herd the city owns — hence the separate ids.
  // The display name repeats the name of the raw resource on purpose: the
  // player raises the same animal.
  //
  // The price repeats the price of the corresponding wild animal: a live
  // animal is worth at least as much as the one on the range, and the city
  // herd on the storage IS the wealth of the species (the slaughterhouse
  // never touches the breeding core of 10 heads, see game_balance.json).
